/E (Mission Statement)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 486 0 R
/E (The State of the Girl Report exists because data has the power to drive change, but only when it is gathered with intention, interpreted with integrity, and shared in service of the girls it represents. This report is more than a collection of statistics. It is a commitment to seeing girls fully: their strengths, their challenges, and the structural conditions that shape their lives from early childhood through young adulthood.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 486 0 R
/E (Girls across Washington State navigate school and healthcare systems that were not always designed for them, unintentionally overlooking their unique needs and potential. This report names opportunities for improvement as an initial step towards better representing girls in Washington.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 486 0 R
/E (When communities, policymakers, and educators can see where girls are thriving and where they are falling behind, they are better equipped to make decisions that reflect the full picture. Disaggregated and accessible data allows for a deeper understanding of which populations are needing more support.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 486 0 R
/E (The girls of Washington are already demonstrating extraordinary resilience. They are graduating, leading, and advocating for one another despite persistent structural barriers. This report honors that resilience while opening the door for positive impact. The goal is to increase awareness and action with this report for every girl, in every community in Washington State.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
