548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 488 0 R
/E (Structural barriers accumulate. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
549 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 488 0 R
/E (The challenges documented in this report are cumulative and interconnected. A girl in a rural, low-income district faces limited access to healthcare and limited exposure to career pathways. A girl in foster care enters adolescence already managing elevated mental health needs before any individual choices are made. Girls' strong academic performance cannot explain Washington's 6th-largest wage gap; it is explained by the structural conditions that determine which opportunities become available. Improving outcomes for Washington girls requires addressing these structural barriers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
550 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 488 0 R
/T (Girls are increasingly engaged in school, but not all girls feel they belong.)
/E (Girls are increasingly engaged in school, but not all girls feel they belong.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
551 0 obj
<<
