/P 490 0 R
/T (Physical Health Risks and Trends Many girls in Washington are not meeting key physical health benchmarks.       Data from the Washington Healthy Youth Survey shows that only 38% of 10th grade girls meet the recommended 60 minutes of daily physical activity. Early health experiences also matter: over one-third of youth report at least one Adverse Childhood Experience \(ACE\), which can influence health outcomes and sense of safety. Health outcomes vary across communities. Access to healthcare services is not evenly distributed across Washington, with rural areas facing fewer healthcare providers and longer travel distances to care.)
/E (Physical Health Risks and Trends Many girls in Washington are not meeting key physical health benchmarks.       Data from the Washington Healthy Youth Survey shows that only 38% of 10th grade girls meet the recommended 60 minutes of daily physical activity. Early health experiences also matter: over one-third of youth report at least one Adverse Childhood Experience \(ACE\), which can influence health outcomes and sense of safety. Health outcomes vary across communities. Access to healthcare services is not evenly distributed across Washington, with rural areas facing fewer healthcare providers and longer travel distances to care.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
