/E (Career Pathways Reflect Occupational Segregation Girls are concentrated in Career and Technical Education \(CTE\) pathways tied to care, education, and service fields associated with lower lifetime earnings. They remain underrepresented in STEM, trades, and technical programs that lead to higher wages and credential completion within six years after graduation.)
