1047 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (The Washington State of the Girl Report compiles metrics across five core areas: Physical Health, Emotional Well-being, Social/Behavioral Health, Academic/Career Readiness, and Safety. Data visuals present comparisons and disparities across grade levels, sexual orientations, race and ethnicity, disability status, foster care involvement, and geographic regions using publicly available state and national sources.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1048 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Data Collection )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1049 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Data sources include the Washington State Healthy Youth Survey, Communities Count, Washington State Department of Health, Washington State Health Care Authority, Washington State Department of Social and Health Services, Office of Superintendent of Public Instruction, CDC YRBS, CDC WONDER, Washington Tracking Network, Child and Adolescent Health Measurement Initiative, Education Research and Data Center, and the Status of Women in Washington report. All data is anonymized; no primary research was conducted.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1050 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Agency Data )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1051 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (This report cites national research for context across all five content areas: CDC YRBS and WONDER for Physical Health; the Trevor Project \(2023\) for Emotional Well-being and Safety; peer-reviewed ACEs research and social media data for Social/Behavioral Health; national wage gap research for Academic/Career Readiness; and Stop AAPI Hate \(2023\) for disaggregated AAPI Safety data. Cited research is contextual only and does not replace Washington-specific data.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1052 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (Disaggregating Data)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1053 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 512 0 R
/E (To understand differences among girls in Washington, data are disaggregated by grade level, sexual orientation, race, ethnicity, disability status, foster care involvement, and county where available. The ability to disaggregate is limited by the availability of statewide data; this report acknowledges its inability to fully capture all intersectionalities of the target audience.                                         )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
